Applied by build.sh on top of the iPXE checkout, in name order.

bzimage-initrd-below-4g.patch
  On BIOS, iPXE keeps initrds below the kernel's initrd_addr_max, which is 2 GB even for
  kernels that accept initrds anywhere (XLF_CAN_BE_LOADED_ABOVE_4G). With the patch those
  kernels get the whole 32-bit space, so a 2-3 GB live image carried in the initramfs (MX)
  also boots on BIOS machines.
